# JacRed Mintlify documentation

- Treat application code, `Configuration/AppOptions.cs`, `Configuration/Schema/ConfigSchema.cs`, `Data/crontab`, `Data/init.yaml`, `Data/example.yaml`, and `web/public/openapi.yaml` as the source of truth. Public DeepWiki is not a source of truth; do not copy MDX into `.devin/wiki.json` (30-page public cap).
- Write user-facing content in Russian with direct, active language and sentence-case headings.
- Every MDX page must have `title`, `sidebarTitle`, `description`, and useful `keywords`.
- Use root-relative internal links without the `/docs/` prefix and without `.mdx`.
- Keep `docs.json`, `.mintignore`, and `AGENTS.md` in `docs/`. Add every new page to `docs.json`; preserve existing slugs or add a redirect.
- Load Mintlify skills from `.agents/skills/` (`mintlify`, `mintlify-docs`, `mintlify-api`) and MCP servers from `.cursor/mcp.json`.
- Use Mintlify components only when they improve scanning: `Steps` for procedures, `Tabs`/`CodeGroup` for alternatives, callouts for risk, and `ParamField`/`ResponseField` for API contracts.
- Give every code fence a language and keep examples runnable against port `9117`.
- Never publish real API keys, tokens, passwords, cookies, wallet secrets, or private URLs.
- Distinguish C# `AppOptions` defaults, packaged `Data/init.yaml`, and full `Data/example.yaml`. Never mix them silently.
- Document `/dev/*` and destructive maintenance actions as operator-only features with warnings.
- Do not describe retired tracker icons as active trackers.
- Before completion, run `mint validate`, `mint broken-links --check-anchors`, and `mint a11y` from `docs/`.
